    "summary": "## Implementation Summary: KIP-1319 - Align TxnOffsetCommit API with OffsetCommit API\n\nSuccessfully implemented support for topic IDs in the TxnOffsetCommit API to align it with the OffsetCommit API.\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n**1. TxnOffsetCommitResponse.java**\n- Added `Uuid` import to support topic ID handling\n- Added `newBuilder(boolean useTopicIds)` method that returns either `TopicIdBuilder` (for topic IDs) or `TopicNameBuilder` (for topic names)\n- Kept backward-compatible `newBuilder()` method that defaults to `TopicNameBuilder`\n- Enhanced abstract `Builder` class with `topicId` parameter in abstract methods\n- Added overloaded `addPartition()` and `addPartitions()` methods:\n  - Old 3-parameter and 4-parameter versions for backward compatibility\n  - New 4-parameter and 5-parameter versions that accept topicId\n- Added new `TopicIdBuilder` class that uses topic IDs as the primary key for organizing response topics\n- Updated `TopicNameBuilder` to accept topicId and set it on response topics\n\n**2. TxnOffsetCommitRequest.java**\n- Updated static `getErrorResponse()` method to preserve topic IDs from request to response\n- Updated static `getErrorResponseTopics()` method to include topic IDs in response topics\n\n### Key Features:\n- Full backward compatibility with existing code\n- Support for both topic ID and topic name based builder patterns\n- Topic IDs are properly preserved in error responses\n- Aligns with OffsetCommit API design patterns\n- All tests pass successfully\n\n### Test Results:\n✅ All TxnOffsetCommitRequestTest tests pass\n✅ All TxnOffsetCommitResponseTest tests pass\n✅ Backward compatible with existing code that doesn't use topic IDs"
  },
